# PATCH: 015-strip-blocked-args
#
# Enforce a fail-closed Windows launch contract
#
# PURPOSE:
#   Make Firefox's existing same-binary Windows launcher mandatory for every
#   public DenBrowser start. The launcher accepts only the canonical public
#   grammar, constructs a clean OS-derived environment for the real browser,
#   and transfers an in-memory authorization value before resuming it.
#
# PUBLIC GRAMMAR:
#   denbrowser.exe
#   denbrowser.exe -osint -url http(s)://...
#   The exact advisory -os-restarted prefix is also accepted for Windows
#   Restart Manager, but never widens the grammar or environment contract.
#
# SECURITY PROPERTIES:
#   - Unknown, duplicated, reordered, inline, and alternate-spelling arguments
#     reject the entire invocation with exit code 127; nothing is stripped.
#   - -app, -xpcshell, logging aliases, automation, debug, profile, and test
#     entry points are unreachable from a public launch.
#   - The browser receives only OS-derived SystemRoot/SystemDrive/Path,
#     LOCALAPPDATA/TEMP/TMP, and ProgramFiles values. No caller-provided MOZ,
#     XRE, XPCOM, NSS, proxy, logging, debugging, or loader variable survives.
#   - Genuine Gecko children require canonical -contentproc placement and an
#     actual same-binary parent. Browser restarts re-enter the same launcher,
#     but routing markers never authorize MOZ/XRE state projection.
#   - Launcher errors fail closed; registry crash fallback cannot enter the
#     browser in-process.
#
# WINDOWS SCOPE:
#   The lightweight first launcher still begins under the caller's loader
#   environment. The real browser has a clean environment from process birth.
#   Eliminating the first-process loader residual would require an external
#   protected launcher, intentionally outside this Firefox-only design.


